{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/556261-wolves-in-new-york","id":556261,"title":"Wolves in New York","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-15T17:35:11-07:00","id":556261,"title":"Wolves in New York","content":"So while Bowery Dogs is real cool, it only gives you a loose idea of what New York's wolf scene is like in the 1970's. I'm wondering, does anyone have any suggestions or interesting ideas on what the situation might be for the Wolves of New York modernly? Do you think there's a lot of Pure here, or that the Uratha were wiped out? Etcetera. I'm hunting for any kinds of interesting, broad ideas to work with, if anyone has done anything for their modern New York.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T17:55:14-07:00","id":556300,"title":"","content":"I think it's the middle or beginning of the Brethren War, but dates for that are a bit weird, especially considering how time has changed since the first book. So I'd probably lead up to that.<br /> <br /> During the Brethren War, the Pure were apparently thought to be fewer in number, but had actually been spreading their faith in the wilds, while the Forsaken were sort of getting fat and sloppy and resorting to in-fighting more than usual. I guess I'd have Pure be few and far between, the Ivory Claws probably have some holdouts in New York, what with some old lineages there, and the Fire-Touched are probably getting into the swing of things with the drug problem rising, it's easy to imagine a Charles Manson-like Fire-Touched getting people all doped up and cultish to their beliefs. Predator Kings might take advantage of the police corruption to hunt some of the more straight-arrow ones and if the Forsaken are strong in number, Predator Kings could make some pretty infamous names for themselves by hunting them.<br /> <br /> I think the Forsaken would be strongest in New York, with the Bale Hounds having a lot of influence of their own, using first edition's concept of Bale Hounds as living purveyors of sin, New York seems to be the place for it. Maybe, just like the city, the Forsaken would be sort of torn between the old and the young, with a lot of youngsters who want more but are constantly held back by the elders.<br /> <br /> Apparently until the Brethren War, the Pure never had a strong hold in the 'new world,' so I'd really play down the danger of the Pure as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-15-2015, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:41:30-07:00","id":556520,"title":"","content":"I was speaking about modern New York, not New York in the 70's. I'm looking for ideas on what New York might look like as a territory circa 2015.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:48:26-07:00","id":556528,"title":"","content":"Man I totally misread that. Right there, second line, modernly. Then the third line just out and out modern.<br /> <br /> Eh. I'd probably cut back on the Predator Kings, keep prestigious Ivory Claws in certain areas, Fire-Touched trying to get in through the religious angles, but overall more heavy on the Forsaken and Bale Hound populations. My old werewolf game was in New York,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/251268-favorite-werewolf-antagonist-stories?p=252566#post252566\"> there were a bunch of nasty Pure and Forsaken packs</a> and other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:05:26-07:00","id":559977,"title":"","content":"If you are talking about after the Brethren war and subsequent pure uprising I think there would be a lot of forsaken hiding in New York and I do mean hiding. Even those who have rebuilt their strength and confidence would have a siege mentality. I also think the forsaken packs of the city would hold strong ties to each other, a normal side effect of the 'us vs them' view of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T23:09:20-07:00","id":563754,"title":"","content":"Bone Shadows in Flushing, for sure because of Cypress Hills cemetery, Hamptons belong to the Ivory Claws. Those homeless vets you see? Blood Talons keeping an eye on their streets. Catskills seem like Hunter in Darkness territory, but get too far into the woods and things change. It wasn't a rabid bear that tore up those hunters, the Predator Kings just don't like visitors. There's an awful lot of undeveloped woods still left in NY state, plenty of space for enclaves to form with little contact outside their community. Manhattan itself seem like an Iron Masters paradise, with room for other tribes to carve their niche, certainly the Ivory Claws have their old money businesses with private investment accounts and the Fire Touched have their underground revival meetings in the lower east side. The Ivory Claws won't admit it but they have recently found (and purged) Bale Hounds in their ranks and will readily kill to keep that a secret.<br /> <br /> The fighting over the locus at the Freedom Tower will one day be legendary to the Uratha, but what is the resonance doing to them? This is actually my Maeljin hook for the area, since there are so many different positive emotions and resonance surrounding the building as a monument, but it's surrounded by the highest concentration of greed, gluttony, lust, and pride anywhere in the world (mine anyway). The associated Maeljin are working very hard to keep the others out because they just don't want to share the bounty of Essence, Thurifuge tried and failed to use the Occupy Wall Street movement to gain a foothold but was stopped by the concerted efforts of a number of packs, packs not normally known for working together, and this suits the other Lords of Sin just fine. Hope you find some of this useful","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T14:48:43-08:00","id":823744,"title":"","content":"Necromancy!<br /> <br /> Thank you, Darksider, for speaking to Upstate New York. As someone who lives in the Catskills I can second the most rural parts being dangerous realms of isolation and terror.<br /> <br /> Now I want to know who would be in Queens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:01:20-08:00","id":823754,"title":"","content":"I read <a href=\"http://www.vice.com/read/the-nypd-arrested-15-alleged-gang-members-for-going-on-hunting-expeditions-in-brooklyn\" target=\"_blank\">this article</a> the other day, the headline just stood out to me as a werewolf type thing, though obviously the loss of life isn't something to make light of. Not in Queens, it's a Brooklyn thing, but I imagine a lot of modern werewolves would follow a gang-like structure and social media and technology would be really big. Though obviously you have packs in other groups, from clubs in universities, businesses, law enforcement personnel, religious organizations, tenants associations, or complete strangers.<br /> <br /> There's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gun_Machine\" target=\"_blank\">a book by Warren Ellis, called Gun Machine</a>, that offered to me a twisted depiction of an Iron Master or Predator King who had become entangled with the God Machine in New York. While not about a pack, I could easily see it representing a high Primal Urge, low Harmony lone wolf in the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-04-2016, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}